<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meic Uilleim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as MacWilliams</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Meic Uilleim, or MacWilliams, were descendants of William fitz Duncan, a grandson of Malcolm III, who claimed the Scottish throne. From the 1180s they raised repeated revolts in Moray and Ross against the kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-lion">William the Lion</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a>. The line ended in 1230, when the last known member, an infant girl, was killed at Forfar.</p></div>
